LOCAL PATCH (not submitted anywhere): phy: hisilicon: histb-combphy — allow 32-bit ARM

PHY_HISTB_COMBPHY is gated on ARM64, but the driver is architecture-neutral:
it touches a syscon regmap, a clock and a reset, and contains no 64-bit
assumptions. The SoCs it serves are Cortex-A53, which also run AArch32, and
the stock bootloader on at least one retail Hi3798CV200 box is a 32-bit U-Boot
whose bootm rejects an arm64 image - so a 32-bit kernel is the only way to
boot mainline there without replacing the bootloader.

Dropping the ARM64 condition lets ARCH_HISI on ARCH_MULTI_V7 select it. The
COMPILE_TEST alternative is retained.

--- a/drivers/phy/hisilicon/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/phy/hisilicon/Kconfig
@@
 config PHY_HISTB_COMBPHY
 	tristate "HiSilicon STB SoCs COMBPHY support"
-	depends on (ARCH_HISI && ARM64) || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on ARCH_HISI || COMPILE_TEST
 	select GENERIC_PHY
 	select MFD_SYSCON
 	help
